$ rtok worktree gc --help
Remove merged, clean, idle worktrees with their branches; drop records of deleted ones

Usage: rtok worktree gc [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --config <PATH>            User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --yes                      Apply; without it this is a dry run that changes nothing
      --dry-run                  Say the dry run out loud: print what would go and change nothing
                                 (the default)
      --stat                     The same preview as the dry run: a removal's line already is its
                                 stat
      --owner <OWNER>            Open locks whose reason starts with this owner; any other lock
                                 holds until `--stale-lock`
      --idle <IDLE>              Keep worktrees modified within this window (`24h`, `7d`) [default:
                                 24h]
      --stale-lock <STALE_LOCK>  Treat someone else's lock as abandoned once its merged, clean
                                 worktree is untouched this long [default: 7d]
      --json                     JSON instead of the table
  -h, --help                     Print help

